Day14
Problem statment: Apache (httpd) service is installed on all application server but on one server it is in failed state. Troubleshoot and fix issue with apache (httpd) service
1. Login into application server using below command and provide password once prompted.
        ssh username@host_name
2. Once logged in, check status of httpd service using below command
        sudo systemctl status httpd
3. In my case, the service was failed with error "Address is already in use"                
4. I tried to check if nestat utility is available but it wasn't.
5. Tried installing netstat utility using below command
        sudo yum install net-tools -y
6. Tried to check which service is utilising same address / port using below command
        sudo netstat -tulpn | grep 5001 // Port 5001 because httpd was using same port
7. In output of above command, I got service name as sendmail service being using port 5001.
8. It was misconfiguration for sendmail service hence updated port to 25 in file /etc/mail/sendmail.mc
9. Restarted sendmail service using below command
        sudo systemctl restart sendmail
10. After this tried to restart httpd service using below command
        sudo systemtctl restart httpd
11. Service was able to start and issue was fixed.                                